    "rules": "<b>Choice:</b> Exactly 1 Knight. Max. 2 Outriders, 2 Scouts; max. 5 Chasseurs, 5 Hussars, 2 Grooms.<br><b>Mounted warband:</b> Every warrior comes with a Riding Horse (included in the cost); the Knight, Outriders and Hussars may upgrade it to a Warhorse for +40 gc. All use the Blazing Saddles cavalry rules (Ride / Combat Riding / Horse Handling).<br><b>Horses:</b> A model without a mount may not take part in the battle. Dead horses must be replaced before any other income is spent (treasures are sold to fund this). Enemies may not target a ridden horse, by missiles or in close combat. Any mounted warrior may always be chosen as a target by a shooter even if others are closer, but the shooter gains no +1 to hit.<br><b>Mounted combat:</b> A mounted warrior may not fight with two close combat weapons (he needs one hand for the reins) and may never use two-handed weapons; a shield or buckler is fine, and a pistol may be fired in the first round of close combat in place of a weapon.<br><b>Dense terrain:</b> Imperial Outriders ignore the normal two-mount warband limit in areas of dense terrain.<br><b>Hired Swords:</b> May hire only these Hired Swords, no others – the mounted Freelance Knight (Rulebook) and Roadwarden (Empire in Flames). The Highwayman keeps his distance and may never be hired.",
