  "intro": {
    "text": "When the Nemesis Crown was said to be found, the provinces of the Empire sent fast riders to scout the Great Forest. They avoid head-on fights and rely on speed and stealth to take the prize and be gone.",
    "url": "https://mordheimer.net/docs/warbands/grade-1b-warbands/imperial-outriders"
  },
  "unitLore": {
    "ioknight": "Knights who show the greatest potential are often chosen to lead small bands on quests into dangerous territory in order to prove their worth.",
    "ioout": "Usually the offspring of nobility, Outriders are often cocksure young guns and confident in the saddle. Eager to earn their spurs they readily sign up for dangerous missions requiring speed, stealth and bravery.",
    "ioscoutu": "Accustomed to riding fast over long distances, Empire couriers are an obvious choice to include in raids into the wilder lands. Less experienced at fighting, they need to learn quickly or risk falling at the wayside.",
    "chasseur": "Skilled at firing a range of Blackpowder weapons from the saddle, these men are regarded as the finest young prospects of the Empire’s armies. Chasseurs provide vital missile cover for the band.",
    "hussar": "Selected for their combat skills, these grizzled warriors pack a hard punch as the Outriders charge.",
    "groom": "Unskilled in the ways of war, nevertheless these young men have an empathy with the steeds. Grooms have a vital part to play in their party."
  }
